# ============================================================================
#  addLM - .gitignore
#
#  Both /llama.cpp/ and /models/ ship EMPTY when the project is uploaded.
#  These rules are a SAFETY NET, not a fix for an oversized upload:
#
#    - the launcher downloads ~1.2 GB of llama.cpp binaries into llama.cpp\
#      on the first run, so the folder is full locally even though it is
#      empty in the repo
#    - your .gguf weights land in models\
#
#  Without these rules, a "git add ." after the first launch tries to commit
#  a 551 MB ggml-cuda.dll and the push is REJECTED by GitHub's 100 MB
#  per-file limit. With them, the binaries and weights can never be staged.
# ============================================================================

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# llama.cpp binaries (610 MB extracted, incl. a 551 MB ggml-cuda.dll)
# Downloaded automatically by addLM.ps1 on the first run.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/llama.cpp/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Models - GGUF weights are gigabytes and blow the 100 MB file limit.
# The folder itself is kept via models/.gitkeep so a fresh clone has it.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/models/*
!/models/.gitkeep

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime state written by the launcher (regenerated on every run)
#   llama-server.log             llama.cpp --log-file output
#   opencode.runtime.json        live context/output budget of the server
#   opencode.runtime.actual.json outcome of the last context-sync
#   .models_last_hash.txt        change-detection cache for the model menu
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
scripts/llama-server.log
scripts/opencode.runtime.json
scripts/opencode.runtime.actual.json
scripts/.models_last_hash.txt

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / IDEs / OS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Misc
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*.old

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working document, not part of the published repo.
# Contains the repo-settings text and the private "Before publishing" notes.
# Delete this line if you want to publish the file.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GITHUB_DESCRIPTION.md
